stem:
A beam of electrons is injected horizontally with velocity $v_e = 10^{6}\ \mathrm{m\ s^{-1}}$ into a vacuum tube in which there is a constant electric field $E_0 = 2000\ \mathrm{N\ C^{-1}}$ directed vertically upwards. At the end of the tube the beam hits a fluorescent screen $h = 10\ \mathrm{cm}$ lower than the injection point.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] If the polarity of the field is reversed what happens to the impact point?
\item[(b)] What is the horizontal distance $l$ between the injection point and the screen?
\end{enumerate}

