In the circuit shown in the Figure, the ammeter reading for the current is taken
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] -- with both switches open;
\item[(b)] -- with both switches closed.
\end{itemize}
The readings are the same in the two cases. The power supply $\mathcal{E}$ has negligible internal resistance; using the values $R_1 = 3\,\Omega$, $R_2 = 2\,\Omega$, $R_3 = 3\,\Omega$ and $\mathcal{E} = 12\ \mathrm{V}$, find the resistance $R$.

