An iceberg has the shape of a cube and floats in seawater with $h = 2.5\ \mathrm{m}$ protruding above the surface. The densities of ice, seawater, and fresh water are $\rho_i = 900\ \mathrm{kg\ m^{-3}}$, $\rho_s = 1300\ \mathrm{kg\ m^{-3}}$ and $\rho_f = 1000\ \mathrm{kg\ m^{-3}}$ respectively. Find
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] -- the submerged depth $x_s$ of the iceberg in the sea,
\item[(b)] -- the submerged depth $x_f$ in fresh water.
\end{itemize}
What fraction of the iceberg would be above the surface in the second case?

